+import { cookies } from "next/headers";
+
+/**
+ * First-party hint cookie marking a browser that has completed at least one
+ * successful login. It is NOT auth — WorkOS still fully enforces sessions — it
+ * only lets logged-out marketing surfaces choose between a "Sign in" affordance
+ * (returning visitor) and a "Sign up" affordance (likely new visitor).
+ *
+ * Set on the auth callback's onSuccess (see app/auth/callback/route.ts).
+ */
+export const RETURNING_COOKIE = "ac_returning";
+
+/** Read the returning-visitor hint. Server-only (reads the cookie store). */
+export async function isReturningVisitor(): Promise<boolean> {
+  return (await cookies()).get(RETURNING_COOKIE)?.value === "1";
+}","comments":[{"url":"https://github.[REDACTED:secret.entropy]#issuecomment-4645500817","body":"<h3>[REDACTED:pii.name]</h3>

This PR introduces a non-auth hint cookie (`ac_returning`) that lets logged-out marketing surfaces show "Sign in" to returning visitors and "Sign up" to new ones. The `/auth/login` page becomes dual-mode with adaptive heading, subcopy, toggle link, and a `?error=callback_failed` banner; nav CTAs on the homepage and `MarketingHeader` consolidate to a single `AuthCtaLink` / `authCta()` helper.

- `[REDACTED:secret.entropy].ts` + `onSuccess` hook in the callback route set and read the hint cookie; the `secure` flag is derived from `NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI` to stay consistent with the WorkOS session cookie.
- `AuthCtaLink` / `authCta()` act as the single source of truth for logged-out CTA copy and routing, preventing label drift between the homepage header, hero, and `MarketingHeader`.
- The new `signUpAction` server action and the `mode` prop on `SignInButton` are wired together cleanly; the `returnTo` toggle link correctly preserves non-dashboard redirect targets.

<h3>[REDACTED:pii.name]: 4/5</h3>

Safe to merge — this is a purely additive UX change with no modifications to WorkOS session handling or authorization logic.

The implementation is clean and well-structured. The hint cookie is correctly scoped (httpOnly, lax, domain-consistent with the WorkOS session cookie) and explicitly documented as non-auth. The only gap is that the new sign-up mode test for SignInButton doesn't assert which server action gets called, leaving the mode→action routing branch untested by the test suite.
\[REDACTED:secret.entropy]-in-button.test.tsx could use an additional assertion to verify the correct action is dispatched for sign-up mode.

